{
  "protocol": "wikantik-collab",
  "protocolVersion": 1,
  "source": "docs/MultiEdit.MD sections 0 (A6, A8, A10-A13), 6.1, 6.2 and the Phase 1 plan amendments (Session core, Task 3)",
  "notes": {
    "basePath": "All paths are under /api/collab/{pageName}. Sample page: PageName.",
    "changes": "Every `changes` value is CodeMirror ChangeSet.toJSON(): a number is an unchanged span, [deleted, ...insertedLines] a replacement. Lengths are UTF-16 code units. Sample doc 'Hello world' is 11 units.",
    "reasonOnEvery409": "Every 409 body carries a `reason` (stale-base, rejoin, frozen, publish-merged-retry, not-synced, derived-page). The rejoin 409 also keeps the legacy `rejoin:true`; the stale-base 409 keeps `accepted:false` plus the head `version`, and a stale-base without a numeric `version` is malformed (clients back off, they do not retry immediately).",
    "noPresenceEndpoint": "There is no /presence endpoint (A8). The selection {anchor, head, version, unconfirmed} rides on POST /updates (key `selection`, optional; a push with empty `updates` is a presence-only push). anchor/head are in the sender's LOCAL document coordinates; `version` is the sender's synced version and `unconfirmed` the count of its unconfirmed updates (A12), so a receiver maps them through the corresponding updates.",
    "presence": "AMBIGUITY (6.2 says presence:{...}): chosen as a map keyed by participantId of {displayName, color, anchor, head, version, unconfirmed}, excluding the requester, always the full map of the OTHER LIVE participants (with or without a selection) when `presenceSeq` > the request's presenceSince, else {}. anchor, head, version and unconfirmed are nullable: a participant that has not sent a selection has all four null. A join or leave changes the map (presenceSeq advances). The response carries `presenceSeq`.",
    "cursors": "AMBIGUITY: 6.2 gives GET /updates a presenceSince cursor but no cursor for `events` or a head version. Chosen: response also carries `metaSeq`, `presenceSeq` and `eventSeq`; every event carries a monotonically increasing `seq`; the request adds `eventsSince`. The new head version is `since + updates.length`.",
    "longPoll": "GET /updates parks up to poll.timeoutSeconds. On timeout it answers 200 with empty updates/metaOps/events and presence {}.",
    "join": "join takes priorClientId (the server reissues it when it still knows it, 7.2), initialText and initialMeta (A11; used only when the join creates the session). `doc` is the document at `version`.",
    "ownUpdates": "A pull returns the caller's own updates too; receiveUpdates recognises them by clientID as confirmations. A 200 on POST /updates does NOT remove them; only the pull does.",
    "publish422": "The 422 bodies are those of PageResource.doPut: {error:'frontmatter_validation_failed'|'access_rule_shape'|'math_validation_failed', violations:[...]}. One example is recorded (frontmatter).",
    "errorBodiesWithoutReason": "400 on POST /updates is {reason:'rejected', message} (malformed changes, length mismatch, lone surrogate, clientID not this participant's); 400 on GET /updates is {reason:'bad-since'} (since out of range). 413 is {reason:'oversize'}. 401/403 bodies are the usual RestServletBase error envelope {error, message}, except 403 not-your-participant.",
    "rateLimitedIs429": "Ruling P3: rate-limited is HTTP 429 {reason:'rate-limited', retryAfterMs?} on POST /updates, never 409. retryAfterMs is optional; without it the client uses its own exponential backoff.",
    "participantId": "Every request except join carries `participantId` (the id join returned): in the JSON body for POST endpoints, as a query parameter on GET /updates, and in the pagehide beacon body. The server identifies the participant by it, not by the author key: two tabs of one user are two participants. The id is bound to the author key (A6): another user's participantId answers 403 {reason:'not-your-participant'}; an unknown or expired one answers 409 rejoin; a missing one 400.",
    "presenceOnlyPush": "A push with empty `updates` skips the version check (no stale-base): it only records the selection. A push with updates and version != head is a stale-base 409.",
    "docHash": "DEFERRED, optional: join/pull MAY later carry `docHash` (hash of the document at `version`) so a client can detect divergence. Not part of protocol version 1; clients ignore unknown fields and no case here carries it.",
    "metaEdits": "A14. `metaOps` items on POST /updates are {field, value} (SET; a present `value: null` removes the field), {field, add:\"x\"} (ADD) or {field, remove:\"x\"} (REMOVE). Exactly one of value/add/remove is present, else 400 {reason:'rejected'}; ADD and REMOVE take a string and are allowed only on tags, related and aliases. A push with empty `updates` and non-empty `metaOps` skips the version check (as a presence-only push does). A refused push applies nothing (no text, meta or selection). A push 200 carries `metaSeq`. A pulled meta op is the server-resolved assignment {field, value}, never add/remove, and carries `by` (the author's display name) when a participant authored it; server ops omit `by`.",
    "metaIdempotent": "Every meta edit is idempotent: re-applying a SET of the current value, an ADD of a present item, or a REMOVE of an absent item changes nothing (no metaSeq advance, no pulled op), so a lost acknowledgement and retry is safe. Values are compared as normalised JSON.",
    "renamedSession": "Post-join calls resolve the session by sessionId. The {pageName} path segment may be the session's current name or any name it held earlier; any other name answers 404. A rename emits a page-renamed {to} event.",
    "evicted": "After an `evicted {participantId, reason}` event (reason lost-edit|signed-out|account-deleted) every post-join call by that participant answers 403 {reason:'evicted', detail:<same reason>}. Publishing a frozen draft without createPages answers 403 {reason:'no-create'}. participant-left carries reason left|timeout|evicted. Events: participant-joined {participant}, participant-left {participantId, reason}, external-change {source, pageVersion, version, ranges:[[from,to]], conflictFields:[...], recreated?} (version = collab head right after the server update; ranges in that document's coordinates), page-renamed {to}, page-deleted {}, evicted {participantId, reason}."
  },
